A||||5||Tom88gt||trailer hitch wiring?||||5||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||12-21-2000||10:09 PM||||Just installed my new Fiero Store trailer hitch.  Easy install except for slight triming needed on my Formula's rear facia.<P>Now, how about the wiring?  I can't find any applications at the local auto parts stores.  The guide books that are next to the towing stuff don't list the Fiero.  I'll have to use a generic harness of some type.  Some have a separate 12V power wire, some have some kinda wierd module, some are just a plug and the standard 4 wires that you tap into the car's tail lights.<P>Any suggestions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-21-2000||11:12 PM||||just get access to the backside of tail lights wiring. your harness should have yellow, white, green and black. white will be to a frame ground, green to one of the turn signals, yellow to the other turn signal, black to your regular tail/running lights. wired like this will make all trailer running, signals and brake lights work. You shouldnt need the module type except on newer and foriegn cars.<P>BTW you usually have to change your flasher to a heavy duty or turn sigs will flash too fast.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tom88gt||12-22-2000||02:09 PM||||Thanks, I was hoping just the basic harness was needed cause the brake/tail/turn light are the same bulb.  <P>Never thought about the heavy duty flasher.  Will it make the signals flash slower without the trailer connected?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-22-2000||03:10 PM||||Just get an electronic flasher, it flashes at the same rate no matter what the load.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||12-22-2000||03:48 PM||||electronic flasher?  Finnished wiring.  Flashes a little slower.  Any harm in leaving the stock flasher in place?  Towing will be an occasional thing.||||reg||5
Z||000005||rogergarrison||12-23-2000||08:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tom88gt:<BR><B>electronic flasher?  Finnished wiring.  Flashes a little slower.  Any harm in leaving the stock flasher in place?  Towing will be an occasional thing.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The heavy duty replacemnt look just like the original. It flashes same with or without trailer. If your ok with way the OEM one works, wont hurt a thing to leave it the way it is||||reg||1
